    "turn_text": "God educated, he must have educated Moses that this is the kind of relationship that he wanted and expected. Before we conclude, just one final question, which is actually not related to the Torah text, but a different text. And this is Andrei Melru's 1968 book, Anti-Memoir. Andrei Melru tells the story. He said, I just, I ran into somebody with whom I served in the war, and he said, this man has saved a lot of Jews, and then had become a parish priest. And I said to the priest, in all of your years of hearing confessions, what are two things you've learned about mankind? And the priest said, I've learned two things. One, everyone is much less happy than he seems. And two, there is no such thing as a grown-up person. You want me to comment",
