  {
    "episode_id": 82329,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/2/82329.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 56,
    "turn_text": "So the first thing that I definitely learned in the military is that humans are incredibly right and capable. You know, we cannot understate what we are, what we have inside of us. So men and women come from every corner of the country and display not only mechanical brilliance, not only operational brilliance, but incredible courage, incredible intellectual fortitude, and the opportunity or the capacity to see the entire picture.",
