    "turn_idx": 64,
    "turn_text": "It's one of the reasons why that probably I stayed in the National Guard. Right. That this idea that when you, you're amongst people who have a higher calling, you're amongst people who have a shared culture and a shared sacrifice, there's nostalgia for the simplicity of it all. There's nostalgia for the adrenaline. There's nostalgia for the sense of living in the moment. And there's also no nostalgia for the intellectual aspects of it. Nostalgia for the sense of it. This is something that we never acknowledge, that the idea that you are living and participating in the ultimate form of strategy. And so I'm nostalgic and I miss so much of it.",
